    {
      "id": "PSR-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-power-sum-comparison",
      "title": "Comparing Turán’s lower bound with positive prime moments gives cubic-logarithm repulsion",
      "statement": "Under PSR-01, ΔH≥c₂ log(c₁/(λH³)). For large positive K=log(c₁/(λH³)), failure would force 8^j≤E₀G(j+1)² at some j>αK. Bounded K is covered by the usual zero-free gap.",
      "hypotheses": "Absolute positive constants in PSR-01, the ordinary zero-free gap ΔH≥c_Z/2, and the exceptional bound λ≥c_S/√m. The finite power-sum theorem applies to the retained n≥1 normalized values.",
      "definitions": [
        "u=Δ/w, S=∑Re u, r=16e², ε=1/r, α=1/(2 log r), h=⌈αK⌉."
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "PSR-01"
      ],
